A||||15||kslish||The coolant overfloweth||||1||
Z||000000||kslish||01-02-2001||11:20 AM||||I've got an interesting problem with my GT.  Around three weeks ago my GT's coolant hose running to the thermostat housing burst.  No big deal, replaced the hose and I also replaced the thermostat housing cap and radiator cap with new Stant units(figured it was good preventive maintenance).  I also refilled the coolant and burped the system properly.  <P>This brings us to now.  Lately the coolant overflow bottle has been filling up to near overflowing every time I drive the car a few times.  The car is not overheating at all, but it's almost like the system places coolant into the bottle when the car is run (like it is suppossed to) but it doesn't suck it back in when the car cools off.  As a result the bottle gets more and more coolant in it every time I drive it until the bottle fills up.  I've been removing coolant out of the bottle and refilling it back into the thermostat housing filler neck but that isn't solving the problem obviously.  <P>Anybody have any ideas?  (The radiator is less than two years old also so I'm pretty sure that it is okay and the coolant flow seems to be okay also).  Defective radiator cap maybe?  (How come the recommended replacement Stant unit is rated at 16lbs of pressure instead of the stock caps 15lbs? Will this cause this?)  <P>Ken S.<BR>'87 GT and '86 SC||||reg||1
Z||000001||sqoach||01-02-2001||01:30 PM||||i had a problem kind of similar to yours. i just replaced the cap with a 16 psi. mine originally had a 13 psi cap. it seemed to have fixed the problem. no more overflowing. and radiator caps don't cost much anyway. if you think it might be bad, might as well replace it.<BR>hope this helps.<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||01-02-2001||01:52 PM||||Stant catalogs specify 16lb vented caps. They are wrong. You want 16lb non-vented cap.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||01-02-2001||02:17 PM||||56 is right.  I had the same problem.  The vented cap lets the coolant siphon into the overflow tank if the car is parked with the nose slightly down.  AutoZone lists the vented cap for the Fiero.  That is wrong.  Get the same cap in the non-vented style and your problem should go away.<P>Good luck and Happy New Year,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||01-02-2001||02:17 PM||||56 is right.  I had the same problem.  The vented cap lets the coolant siphon into the overflow tank if the car is parked with the nose slightly down.  AutoZone lists the vented cap for the Fiero.  That is wrong.  Get the same cap in the non-vented style and your problem should go away.<P>Good luck and Happy New Year,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000005||kslish||01-02-2001||02:54 PM||||Anyone got a part number? (preferably a Stant one since that is what most places carry around here).<P>The part number on the cap I have now is 11231 (on the package, it only says 231 on the cap itself).  I assume that is the wrong one.<P>Ken S.<BR>'87 GT and '86 SC<p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 01-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Carrolles||01-02-2001||06:02 PM||||When AutoZone pulled the cap off the rack for me I showed them that it was a vented cap and told them I needed a non-vented one.  They went right to the rack and pulled a non-vented one for me.  I don't have the number handy.   I can pop the hood when I get home and check if you still need the number.||||reg||1
Z||000007||kslish||01-02-2001||07:52 PM||||I could still use the part number if you can check for me.  The closest Autozone is about a 45 minute drive for me even thought they are my favorite parts store, good service and good prices.  <P>Where I live I have Advance Auto and Pep Boys to pick from and their service leaves something to be desired sometimes in my area.  <P>Ken S.<BR>'87 GT and '86 SC||||reg||1
Z||000008||Bob Englert||01-02-2001||09:02 PM||||Don't know that I would drive that far for a radiator cap!  I had the same problem with a cap from Advance.  Got a replacement from NAPA (before I knew the difference between vented and non-vented) and everything has been OK since.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000009||kslish||01-03-2001||12:13 PM||||Oh yeah, forgot about NAPA.  There is one of those across town from me.  I'll try there if nobody can give me a definative Stant part number.  Thanks.<P>Ken S.<BR>'87 GT and '86 SC||||reg||1
Z||000010||TheFiero64||01-03-2001||05:14 PM||||What is a vented cap? Anyone have a picture of the 2 side by side. I wanted to get a crome "be cool" cap from jegs and I don't know if it is vented or not.||||reg||5
Z||000011||theogre||01-03-2001||08:35 PM||||We are refering check valve on the cap. (The little brass disk about the size of a dime.)<P>On the vented one the valve just hangs there. On the non vented cap it has a spring holding it against the rubber seal.<P>both wrenchead and carparts list 10231 not 11231. I have to go to shlep boys and return something. I'll have a look tomorow and see which is which. I'll put the number in my cave as well once we find it.||||reg||1
Z||000012||TheFiero64||01-04-2001||11:19 AM||||Thanks theogre, I always thought those were broken ones and replaced them. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> LOL<BR> <BR>||||reg||10
Z||000013||Motorhead||01-04-2001||05:32 PM||||Ditto on the thanks guys and Ogre!  I've got three or four caps floating around, and still have to wipe up overflow coolant!<BR>Who'da thought the book was wrong!!<BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000014||fiero56||01-04-2001||05:58 PM||||Here is the correct stant part #(don't know if it matters, but it for my '88 v-6 5-speed):<P>230 <BR>16lb release||||reg||1
Z||000015||sqoach||01-04-2001||08:42 PM||||ok so i think i got this. the vented cap has a little dime-sized part on it that's loose? and the non-vented cap doesn't have anything on it that moves (is loose)??<P>the one i just got has the little red handle on it to relieve(sp?) the pressure. i didn't check for vented or non.||||reg||1
